import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a3 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BwzYn71E.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Optimizing the Reactor Crucible Trash Can","description":"","frontmatter":{"head":[["link",{"rel":"canonical","href":"https://kokobird28144.github.io/endfield-skydoc/optimizing-the-reactor-crucible-trash-can"}]],"lang":"en-US","translationSource":{"title":"优化反应池垃圾桶","archivedAt":"2026-10-23T14:20:34.857Z","url":"https://docs.qq.com/aio/DTmluZ1diWlpQZldw?p=4td9eYzMz4ZLGmT0QcTpaQ","scope":"page"}},"headers":[],"relativePath":"optimizing-the-reactor-crucible-trash-can.md","filePath":"logistics/src/page-4td9eYzMz4ZLGmT0QcTpaQ.md","lastUpdated":null}'),n={name:"optimizing-the-reactor-crucible-trash-can.md"};function o(r,e,l,c,p,d){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<div class="logistics-content"><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="优化反应池垃圾桶" aria-hidden="true"></span><h1 id="optimizing-the-reactor-crucible-trash-can" tabindex="-1">Optimizing the Reactor Crucible Trash Can <a class="header-anchor" href="#optimizing-the-reactor-crucible-trash-can" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Optimizing the Reactor Crucible Trash Can&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Source page ID: <code>4td9eYzMz4ZLGmT0QcTpaQ</code> ｜ <a href="https://docs.qq.com/aio/DTmluZ1diWlpQZldw?p=4td9eYzMz4ZLGmT0QcTpaQ" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open in Tencent Docs</a></p></blockquote><p>Traditional crucible trash cans wait until products of several recipes all fill up, triggering blocking clearance. One disposal cycle takes an extremely long time.</p><p>The optimization aims to exploit the crucible&#39;s void slots: occupy a product&#39;s intended slot before the reaction finishes and produces it, preventing its transfer into inventory and triggering blocking clearance.</p><p>After clearance, the original products enter inventory. To handle them, periodically recirculate output until 50 drops accumulate and trigger traditional crucible blocking, or simply use another crucible as a trash can. An Expanded Crucible running several reactions may also implement disposal.</p><p>Experiments currently suggest these Expanded Crucible disposal rules:</p><p>0. Crucibles apparently accept solid input and start reactions only at integer times (liquids are uncertain; other machines may share this behavior). If an item&#39;s actual phase gives a non-integer arrival, the crucible holds it until the next integer time.</p><p>1. Like other machines, a crucible consumes inputs first. After the recipe duration, sufficient available output slots let products enter and complete that production cycle; otherwise the recipe is considered blocked until enough output slots become available. Unlike other machines, every crucible slot may be an output slot.</p><p>2. With no accumulated inventory, different inputs of different recipes can share an input slot, and different recipes&#39; products can share an output slot.</p><p>3. Two or more blocked recipes in an Expanded Crucible can trigger disposal, clearing all items currently inside. Only recipe blocking is required, regardless of whether those recipes&#39; inputs are present.</p><p>4. After disposal, blocked recipe products are not destroyed; they enter the crucible immediately.</p><p>5. For simultaneous external arrivals and completed products, external inputs occupy slots first.</p><p>These rules give the following schemes:</p><p><span id="source-block-gV6UDHqnrjQq9XSlUMomE3"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="无浪费销毁-用于1-5最大净产" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="waste-free-disposal-for-version-1-5-maximum-net-output" tabindex="-1">Waste-Free Disposal (for Version 1.5 Maximum Net Output) <a class="header-anchor" href="#waste-free-disposal-for-version-1-5-maximum-net-output" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Waste-Free Disposal (for Version 1.5 Maximum Net Output)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Waste-free disposal requires no valuable inputs inside the crucible when it triggers. Take a Xircon Expanded Crucible with three recipes:</p><p>1 Xiranite + 1 Clean Water == 1 Liquid Xiranite (2s)</p><p>1 Liquid Xiranite + 1 Sewage == 1 Xircon Effluent + 1 Inert Xircon Effluent (2s)</p><p>2 Xircon Effluent + 1 Ferrium Powder == 1 Xircon + 1 Sewage (2s)</p><p>Reactions 1 and 2 must continue throughout. By rule 5, continuous Xiranite input occupies Liquid Xiranite&#39;s output slot at disposal, destroying that incoming Xiranite before recipe use. Avoiding Xiranite waste therefore requires stopping its input during disposal.</p><p>Besides Sewage to be destroyed, 7 slots remain. Divide the 7 required kinds of miscellaneous material into slot fillers and triggers. Slot fillers enter early without prematurely triggering disposal; triggers enter just before disposal. Slightly excess Clean Water can be a filler. Trigger count is limited above by input-port count; use solids only for easier phase alignment. Its lower limit depends on how many fillers are possible. Experiments show 4 fillers may already trigger disposal in this system. Fewer are safer, so choose 3 fillers and 4 triggers.</p><p>4 triggers require periodically inserting miscellaneous material into the Xiranite belt, giving Xiranite input 30*(T-2)/T u/min. The net-output setup requires at least 13.75 u/min Xircon from this crucible, hence at least 27.5 u/min Xiranite, so T≥24. Sewage requiring disposal is 115.35 u/min (excluding reaction Sewage), and capacity is 50, so T≤20000/769. To fully react all Xircon Effluent each cycle, incoming Xiranite count (T/2-1) must be even. Only T=26s meets all requirements.</p><p>Thus the Xiranite input belt carries 12 Xiranite then 1 miscellaneous item, period 13 items. Fully blocked no-gap Converger mixing cannot construct period 13, so insert uniformly 1/13-rate-limited miscellaneous items into the Xiranite belt. The 4 triggers must enter simultaneously: construct three more 1/13-rate-limited miscellaneous streams, insert one into the Ferrium belt, and phase-align the other two directly into the crucible. The 3 fillers enter through the Clean Water inlet and gaps in the Ferrium belt.</p><p><span id="source-block-y4lFMmpZPZZbTjFmgvLqlo"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="高效销毁-用于芽针-荞花放生机" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="efficient-disposal-for-△" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="高效销毁-用于△" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="efficient-disposal-for-yazhen-buckflower-release-machine" tabindex="-1">Efficient Disposal (for <a href="/endfield-skydoc/yazhen-buckflower-release-machine">Yazhen / Buckflower Release Machine</a>) <a class="header-anchor" href="#efficient-disposal-for-yazhen-buckflower-release-machine" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Efficient Disposal (for [Yazhen / Buckflower Release Machine](page-CJl0m5vqcG6gAnt645AywF.md))&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Traditional release machines jointly make Yazhen Solution and Jincao Solution, triggering disposal through two blocked recipes. Besides Yazhen and Jincao Powder, one Expanded Crucible can accept another belt each of Yazhen and Yazhen Seeds, allowing 150pm Yazhen production count (actually slightly below 150).</p><p>Efficient disposal differs mainly by not requiring continuous reaction: at minimum, one reaction at the disposal event suffices. But all 8 slots must be occupied. Use water + two powders = two solutions as blocking recipes (other reactions basically cannot support high consumption). Both solutions must lack output space at disposal, so supply a little water only when triggering reactions, also consuming accumulated powder.</p><p>Slots therefore are: 1 counted-plant slot, 4 miscellaneous filler slots, 2 powder slots, 1 water slot. The 5 miscellaneous materials need only 1 each at disposal; powders need at least 2 each; water needs at least 3 supplied at disposal, and none otherwise.</p><p>Possible miscellaneous materials: Originium, Ferrium, Ferrium Powder, acid, Sewage (sharing a mixed pipe with acid). Water needs a dedicated inlet so other miscellaneous liquids cannot block it.</p><p>To maximize count farming, divide the 120pm solid-input capacity between miscellaneous items and counted plants. Suppose disposal occurs every 2n seconds. In these 2n seconds, supply 1 each of four miscellaneous materials and 2 each of two powders. With three solid miscellaneous materials and one fluid, 4n-7 counted plants can still enter. Clearly 4n-7&lt;50 gives n&lt;14.25.</p><p>Plant disposal efficiency is (4n-7)/2n=2-7/2n per second =120-210/n per minute. The limit is therefore 105.26/min, corresponding to approximately 210 Yazhen count. Each miscellaneous material then requires 120/57 per minute.</p><p>For footprint comparison, traditional single-core 150pm Yazhen counting needs 3 seed-picking/planting pairs + 1 Expanded Crucible, 1 Shredding Unit, and 1 Seed-Picking Unit. Efficient single-core 210pm counting, ignoring miscellaneous-material and second-powder production, needs 3.5 pairs + 1 Expanded Crucible and 1 Shredding Unit: 40% better at the same footprint. The problem is constructing a mixed belt of 15 Yazhen + 6-point-something miscellaneous + 8-point-something powder, potentially costing many Unloader tiles. Both output solutions must also enter a traditional trash can.</p><p>First-generation thunder machine:</p><p><img src="/endfield-skydoc/logistics/src/assets/images/img-dae8faf1748ee778.q90-711cf24473c28cc2.webp" alt="Optimizing the Reactor Crucible Trash Can"></p><p>MAN, what can I say?</p><p>The intestine-like water/Yazhen paths delay their startup arrivals; that is minor. The main difficulties are first supplying 3 consecutive water every 30 seconds (or instead simultaneously inputting powders to trigger disposal), and second constructing the mixed belt. The image simplifies this with 4/m and 2/m. I could not find a simple 2-way/3-way merging construction for a&gt;4,b&gt;4,c&gt;2,d&gt;2,e&gt;2. (For example, merge three ways, giving ab 1 share each and cde splitting 1 remaining share three ways: 5,5,1.67,1.67,1.67. Alternatively divide 15 into 18 shares, give ab 5 each, then combine the remaining 8 and split them into 3 shares for cde.) This simple version destroys 90pm Yazhen (it should actually reach 106, but the last mixed Yazhen belt still blocked, perhaps a simulator issue).</p><p><img src="/endfield-skydoc/logistics/src/assets/images/img-c521d01aeadc6406.q90-87c97d45f829ffb9.webp" alt="Optimizing the Reactor Crucible Trash Can"></p><p><a href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1w9pv6YEop" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Endfield/AIC: High-Speed Disposal Machine (Every 30s, up to 100/m of One Item)</a></p><blockquote><p>This technology originally saved power by destroying Sewage in the 1.4 maximum-net-output setup. Developers included boss 君 @樊二のいすぼくろ赛高, boss 言, and others. That implementation was more troublesome and apparently everyone stayed too busy to finish it. My cursed Yazhen-release research instead produced this high-speed version (</p></blockquote><p>[Yazhen Release Machine MK.II] share code EF01o5u1U7OA061UIieO<br> Before connecting the water conduit, pour in 1 drop of Sewage and let it circulate.<br> Connect one water pump and one acid pump to the conduits; actual demand is far lower. The 3 miscellaneous materials can be replaced, as can acid with another liquid: just occupy 4 slots. Avoid materials such as Xiranite that react with water.</p><p>The theoretical limit should be 106 destroyed per minute, leaving 14: powders take 4+4, and miscellaneous materials 2+2+2. That splitting structure is awkward. The video&#39;s 100 version is much simpler.</p><p>Uses orirock&#39;s flow regularizer to output 3 consecutive water every 30 seconds <a href="/endfield-skydoc/flow-regularizer">Flow Regularizer</a>.</p><p>[Yazhen Release Machine MK.II] share code EF01o5u1U7OA061UIieO</p><p>Usage: <strong>after placement, put 1 drop of Sewage into the water conduit before connecting the water and acid pumps</strong>. Preferably open the fourth port&#39;s Control Port only after stabilization. Handle the two output solutions. The three miscellaneous materials are replaceable. Remember to produce both powders elsewhere.</p><p>Below is 乾震&#39;s improved version. Acid blocking triggers output of 3 water and hence disposal; filling the 2 produced medicinal solutions then triggers input of 2 medicinal powders and miscellaneous materials, effectively adjusting speed automatically. These architectures illustrate the distinction between timing control and blocking control.</p><p>Automatic high-speed disposal machine: EF01u28I5E12805a1AoOU</p><p><a href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1VTp36mESS" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cursed Engineering Basics: Automatic High-Speed Disposal Machine</a></p><blockquote><p>Sigh, I did not really want to publish it: people would say “still too useful”... But my conscience would not let me hide it, so I edited a simple video. Use it quietly; do not spread it—or modify it beyond recognition first.</p></blockquote><p>Based on @蓝海露花_kokobird&#39;s BV1w9pv6YEop, itself based on power-saving Sewage disposal for 1.4 maximum net output, developed with @樊二のいすぼくろ赛高, 言, and others. Their device was so useful that even making mine more cursed still leaves it useful—but absolutely not because my modifications are useful!</p><p>Automatic high-speed disposal machine: EF01u28I5E12805a1AoOU</p><p>The boss has updated it yet again...</p><p><a href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1WBp76SEUi" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cursed Engineering Basics: Super-Speed Sewage Treatment Plant</a></p><blockquote><p>Regarding the previous BV1VTp36mESS, someone asked me last night to try the theoretical limit, so I tested it after a simple modification. Limited by the Clean Water input rate, the Sewage disposal ceiling is about 190, so I simply designed it for a stable disposal limit of 180~</p></blockquote><p>Based on @蓝海露花_kokobird&#39;s BV1w9pv6YEop, which was designed to save power by disposing of Sewage in the 1.4 maximum-net-output setup. Development involved 君 @樊二のいすぼくろ赛高, 言, and others. Their device was so useful that, even after I made it this cursed, it still looks reasonably respectable—absolutely not because my modifications are useful!</p><p>Super-Speed Sewage Treatment Plant: EF0193a6I8A3aeO6i5uI2</p><p><span id="source-block-djI0fsbTZuU6JJ46fwu8c1"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="高效壤晶污水处理" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="efficient-xircon-sewage-treatment" tabindex="-1">Efficient Xircon Sewage Treatment <a class="header-anchor" href="#efficient-xircon-sewage-treatment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Efficient Xircon Sewage Treatment&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Because of rule 4, Sewage might be destroyed inside the Xircon crucible without wasting reaction products. Investigate whether the theory holds and what input patterns it needs.</p><blockquote><p>Translation note: The source first lists four miscellaneous filler slots, then refers to “5 miscellaneous materials”; this discrepancy is preserved. Chinese embedded in images has not been redrawn.</p></blockquote></div>',1)])])}const m=i(n,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
